+# Full study — S5-CLM-00003496
+
+## Frozen provenance
+
+The selected workset member is
+`Arxiv.«2001.02665».kotzig_conjecture_large`, revision
+`2270d31e8dd611521f979de6d86da364930b7669`, with exact record digest
+`a7fffb4ef86c261a22b1c3abd41e4973176cf9c06b66c66badde58c24260508b`.
+Its declaration asserts the large-n cyclic decomposition theorem. The provider
+body is a `sorry`, so it is rejected as proof authority. This node supplies only
+the proposition and feeds the identity and transport nodes. If the provider
+bytes, declaration range, revision, or member record changes, the anchor is
+invalid. Trust boundary: frozen source bytes identify the claim but prove
+nothing.
+
+## Exact statement identity
+
+Assume the active symbols retain their `Mathlib` meanings and no local
+declaration, notation, macro, coercion, alias, or substitute import shadows the
+surface. The target repeats every binder, hypothesis, witness component and
+conclusion in the frozen declaration type. Reflexivity of `↔` therefore yields
+the bidirectional crosswalk. The output is exact proposition identity and it is
+used by both transports and the audit. Exceptional case: changing even one
+clause, including the cyclic equation or complete-graph equality, invalidates
+identity. Trust boundary: Master independently re-elaborates both expressions.
+
+## Forward transport
+
+Hypothesis: a proof of the exact frozen proposition is explicitly supplied.
+Because the target proposition is definitionally the same, returning that proof
+establishes the target surface. The output feeds the audit. The provider theorem
+body is not supplied and is never referenced; a hidden application to the
+sorry-backed declaration would violate the trust census. Trust boundary: the
+visible premise carries all mathematical proof responsibility.
+
+## Reverse transport
+
+Hypothesis: a proof of the claim-owned proposition is explicitly supplied.
+Returning it at the definitionally identical frozen surface establishes the
+reverse direction and feeds the audit. No provider body is unfolded and no
+exception is silently handled. Trust boundary: kernel-visible definitional
+transport only.
+
+## Audit and release boundary
+
+Assume every proposition clause, proof premise, dependency and trust boundary
+above remains present. The audit checks exact identity and that transport adds
+no hidden inference. Its output is a complete worker evidence package with
+empty human and readability cuts. The structured machine candidate records
+empty machine cuts, but the worker's permitted validator does not invoke Lean;
+therefore final unconditional exact-root M0 closure and canonical release are
+reserved for Master. Exceptional case: a passing worker preflight alone never
+sets `master_accepted=true`. Trust boundary: only Master can integrate, compile,
+recompute, and advance the Blueprint item.
+
+## Mathematical interpretation
+
+For sufficiently large `n`, take any finite tree with `n` edges. The witness is
+a family of embeddings into the cyclic vertex set of size `2n+1`. Every member
+is obtained by adding its index to a base embedding. Their mapped trees have
+pairwise disjoint edge sets, and their supremum equals the top simple graph, so
+they partition all edges of the complete graph. The statement is strictly
+stronger than merely asking for unrelated copies: the cyclic-shift equation is
+part of the output and cannot be omitted.
